dot · manage this machine, its shell, its agents and its configuration

Usage: dot <domain> [object] <verb> [args]

CONFIGURATION
  config     apply, diff and sync the dotfiles
  shell      aliases, history, startup caches
  theme      one palette for every app
  tool       toolchains, packages, project templates

SESSIONS
  session    find, open and restore terminal sessions
  top        what the machine and its agents are doing

AGENTS
  ai         install, route and run coding agents
  agent      modes, policy, sandbox, budgets
  mcp        MCP servers as supply chain

SYSTEM
  system     updates, cleanup, scheduled maintenance
  doctor     health, repair, backup and rollback

TRUST & HOSTS
  secret     secrets, keys and SSH certificates
  security   OS hardening
  attest     attestation and verification
  fleet      many hosts

PLATFORM
  cli        plugins, updates, completions
  ui         primitives for scripts

SHORTCUTS
  apply      dot config apply
  sync       dot config sync
  diff       dot config diff
  status     dot config status
  edit       dot config edit
  cd         dot config path
  update     dot system update

Run 'dot help <domain>' for its commands, 'dot help all' for every command,
'dot help <term>' to search, 'dot help --json' for the catalog. Version 0.2.536.
